+ * what QEMU shows, the window is what SDL was asked for, and the drawable is what the
+ * guest's GL context really renders into. They drift apart in full screen, because
+ * SDL_SetWindowSize() is documented to do nothing there -- "Fullscreen windows
+ * automatically match the size of the display mode". Printed only when something
+ * changes, otherwise it would arrive once per presented frame.
