+ * walks out of the window, which is what the user sees. Ask SDL, say so, and put it
+ * right. Idempotent, so it can be called from every event that could have disturbed it.
+ */
+/* The window grab alone does not confine the pointer on this host: measured 17 times in
+ * one session, the pointer left the window while QEMU *and* SDL both reported the grab as
+ * held, and grab_resync() never found a disagreement to fix (docs/LOG.md [396]).
+ *
+ * Relative mouse mode is the mechanism SDL keeps working for exactly this: it hides the
+ * cursor, holds it in place and delivers nothing but deltas -- which is what a guest with
+ * a PS/2 mouse wants anyway. QEMU's SDL front end only ever switches it off, never on.
+ *
+ * QEMU_3DFX_RELATIVE_MOUSE=0 falls back to the window grab alone.
+ */
